<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	No App Sandbox: Pelican runs /usr/bin/nettop and /usr/bin/log (bluetoothd's log, for the
	Radios screen); loads NetworkStatistics.framework and libIOReport (the radio drivers'
	counters); reads other apps' bundles and code signatures; and caches HuggingFace models under
	the user's home. When asked to switch a wired service off it runs /usr/bin/osascript, which
	asks macOS for a one-off authorization — no privileged helper is installed and nothing of the
	authorization is kept. No Bluetooth usage key: Pelican never uses CoreBluetooth, so it never
	asks for Bluetooth permission.
	No hardened-runtime exceptions: everything is statically linked, and MLX compiles its Metal
	kernels through the Metal compiler service, not writable+executable CPU pages.
	Add keys here (not on the codesign command line) so make-app.sh and make-pkg.sh pick them up.
	-->
</dict>
</plist>
